        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "A shutout silence has swallowed the Toronto Blue Jays, and the momentum they barely grasped against the Mets has evaporated into thin air. <strong>The Jays fell to the Mets 3-0</strong> on Tuesday night, a deadening blow that extends their losing streak to one and leaves them mired at 40-46, third in the AL East and 11 games behind the division leader. The bullpen imploded again, while Gausman's rare bounce-back effort - seven shutout innings, 10 strikeouts on 88 pitches - went unrewarded as the offense produced zero runs, a stark contrast to the 2-1 victory the day before. Vladdy's struggles continue to haunt the lineup, and the team's -3.0 point differential screams of a squad that can't sustain contention energy. With the season slipping, the focus shifts to whether this roster can regroup before the wild card race tightens further. <strong>Wednesday's rematch with the Mets at 2:07 PM ET</strong> is the next critical test - can the Jays break the shutout cycle and reclaim any hope of a comeback?",
